{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/651593-why-do-you-like-steven-universe","id":651593,"title":"Why do you like Steven Universe?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-04T12:03:51-07:00","id":651593,"title":"Why do you like Steven Universe?","content":"I just completed the series and I love it to bits. I think it might replace MLP:FiM as the second best animated series for kids and young adults that I've seen (the top spot still securely held by Avatar: the Last Airbender).<br /> <br /> There are many reasons to like it, but I think the biggest one for me is that there's a really strong sense of complexity and layers. The show makes me feel comfortable assuming that Things will Matter in the same way Avatar did and which MLP sadly fails at most of the time. The world feels <i>deep</i>, not just big, and that goes for the characters as well, of course. Aside from in a literal sense, the characters both take up much space in the intrigue and feel like they're grounded, fleshed out and very unique. It's not just a bunch of aliens with different personalities, they're also given genuinely different situations and problems that we actually get to see them grapple with.<br /> <br /> Naturally, there's also the progressive aspects of the series, which are very nice.<br /> <br /> One thing I'm worried about is the schedule, though. From what I understand, it's been pretty sparse and erratic? There's a hiatus right now, and I'm not sure when it'll end. With the episode being ten minutes, it might feel like too little, too thin.<br /> <br /> Edit: That title, though... it seems I can't edit it. Well, that's what the thread is called I guess!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 09-04-2015, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T12:53:45-07:00","id":651673,"title":"","content":"I need to watch this series.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T13:21:31-07:00","id":651736,"title":"","content":"I started this very recently (just saw episodes 3 and 4 yesterday). I admit I feel like I'm still just settling into its rhythm, much like I was with Adventure Time at that point. That said, I'm enjoying myself so far; it has a good vibe to it. I don't have much else to say at this point, but hopes run high.<br /> <br /> Between it and catching up with the episodes of Gravity Falls that came out these last few months (never mind Adventure Time and MLP), this has been a pretty great time for animation aimed at this age group. ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T14:04:22-07:00","id":651769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/651593-why-do-you-like-steven-universe?p=651673#post651673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I need to watch this series.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you'd really like it. There are 67 episodes so far, but they're only about 10 minutes each, so it doesn't take that long to get caught up.<br /> <br /> I suppose I can't really direct you to any specific place to watch it though, since y'know, rules. :/<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/651593-why-do-you-like-steven-universe?p=651736#post651736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I started this very recently (just saw episodes 3 and 4 yesterday). I admit I feel like I'm still just settling into its rhythm, much like I was with Adventure Time at that point. That said, I'm enjoying myself so far; it has a good vibe to it. I don't have much else to say at this point, but hopes run high.<br /> <br /> Between it and catching up with the episodes of Gravity Falls that came out these last few months (never mind Adventure Time and MLP), this has been a pretty great time for animation aimed at this age group. ^_^</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's pretty good right now! I've been glancing at Gravity Falls myself, but I haven't watched it yet.<br /> <br /> Adventure Time... never got into it. I can see the appeal, but it was a bit much &quot;lulz teh randoms&quot; for me. Even if the randomness was backed up by interesting points, it just didn't catch me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T14:31:44-07:00","id":651792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/651593-why-do-you-like-steven-universe?p=651769#post651769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it's pretty good right now! I've been glancing at Gravity Falls myself, but I haven't watched it yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>It comes highly recommended. ^__^ You'd also have the advantage of the series not pausing for several months on a cliffhanger. Though, given the staggered pacing of new episodes, I may be speaking too soon. &gt;.&gt; Still two more to watch myself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Adventure Time... never got into it. I can see the appeal, but it was a bit much &quot;lulz teh randoms&quot; for me. Even if the randomness was backed up by interesting points, it just didn't catch me. </div> </div> </div>Aye, I can get that; it's certainly not for everyone. It took me quite a few episodes before I started to really enjoy it. What may have helped me get into it was watching along with Doug Walker's vlogs,* as that gave me another reason to watch until I got into it for its own sake. If nothing else, I remember <a href=\"http://channelawesome.com/adventure-time-vlogs-slumber-party-panic/\" target=\"_blank\">his first one</a> being fairly entertaining.<br /> <br /> * As I'm actually also doing with Steven Universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Tidied up response. 09-04-2015, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T14:43:15-07:00","id":651799,"title":"","content":"Oh, I didn't know he was doing vlogs of SU. I loved his Avatar vlogs. I'll need to check that out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T14:49:27-07:00","id":651802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/651593-why-do-you-like-steven-universe?p=651799#post651799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I didn't know he was doing vlogs of SU. I loved his Avatar vlogs. I'll need to check that out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aye, I really dug those, too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If I hadn't enjoyed them so much, I might not have given Adventure Time the sort of shot that I did. I'm enjoying his Steven Universe vlogs with Rob, as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T15:43:30-07:00","id":651836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/651593-why-do-you-like-steven-universe#post651593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I'm worried about is the schedule, though. From what I understand, it's been pretty sparse and erratic? There's a hiatus right now, and I'm not sure when it'll end. With the episode being ten minutes, it might feel like too little, too thin.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has to do with the way the show is made. They're short episodes, so two can be shown in a single block, and Cartoonnetwork can run them in different combinations. Typically they pair one new(er) episode with one older one. There are long stretches of no new episodes while the creators work, then once they've finished a good chunk, those episodes get added to the list that Cartoonnetwork can run, and those of us who wait for the new episodes and watch them as soon as they're out get a week or so of a new episode every day, rather than several weeks of one new episode a week.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/651593-why-do-you-like-steven-universe#post651593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: That title, though... it seems I can't edit it. Well, that's what the thread is called I guess!</div> </div> </div> </div>I can change it if you like. Just let me know what you want it to be called.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-04-2015, 06:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T07:10:41-07:00","id":652440,"title":"","content":"1) For those of you interested in picking up the show, Steven's a little too far on the &quot;obnoxious child&quot; end for a lot of adult cartoon lovers when the show opens. I recommend watching &quot;Bubble Buddies&quot;, &quot;Giant Woman&quot;, and the three Lion episodes to help decide if the show intrigues you.<br /> <br /> 2) The hiatus ends Thursday, September 10, AKA Thursday. Basically Cartoon Network rotates which shows are airing new episodes. I have no idea why, but they seem to think it's good for business.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T08:21:46-07:00","id":652571,"title":"","content":"The rotation lets them build the hype train and keeps people regularly watching the channel as opposed to having high points and low points. Also it probably gives them a better feel for what shows are doing well and which aren't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T18:17:42-07:00","id":653303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/651593-why-do-you-like-steven-universe?p=651836#post651836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can change it if you like. Just let me know what you want it to be called.</div> </div> </div> </div>Appreciate it. I was aiming for &quot;Why do you like Steven Universe?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/651593-why-do-you-like-steven-universe?p=652440#post652440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) The hiatus ends Thursday, September 10, AKA Thursday. Basically Cartoon Network rotates which shows are airing new episodes. I have no idea why, but they seem to think it's good for business.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh nice! That means both SU and MLP will return shortly. I'll be busy!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/651593-why-do-you-like-steven-universe?p=652571#post652571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rotation lets them build the hype train and keeps people regularly watching the channel as opposed to having high points and low points. Also it probably gives them a better feel for what shows are doing well and which aren't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand the first and last points, but wouldn't rotation like that create exactly the kind of behaviour where people watch in bursts, instead of continuously? It seems that if you like the one show, you'd be incentivised to watch one out four weeks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T17:40:23-07:00","id":660129,"title":"","content":"There are so many reasons I like this show, that I can hardly separate them all.<br /> <br /> I mean, I like how it all strings together. Despite being episodic, all the stories feel interconnected, unlike some shows where the events of some episodes may as well have never happened. If not the world itself, they all feel like they have an impact on the characters and their personalities.<br /> I like the characters. From the Gems, who can feel mysterious and otherworldly just as often as they feel funny and relatable. To the Humans, who all have their little quirks and depths. I think my favourite has to be Pearl, because all of how her flaws and virtues blend together to make her so complicated and interesting.<br /> I like the world. There is so much mystery and it's all revealed at a great pace, which gives you just enough time to try and figure things out before the curtain is lifted. It fuels speculation and makes me more curious to find out more about the world the show is set in.<br /> <br /> It's quickly becoming my favourite show, but it hasn't surpassed Avatar yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T07:51:33-07:00","id":660696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose I can't really direct you to any specific place to watch it though, since y'know, rules</div> </div> </div> </div> Arcane is American; he can watch it legally on Cartoon Network's website. Look, it's <a href=\"http://www.cartoonnetwork.com/video/steven-universe\" target=\"_blank\">right here</a>. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recommend watching &quot;Bubble Buddies&quot;, &quot;Giant Woman&quot;, and the three Lion episodes to help decide if the show intrigues you.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh don't do that. Most of those episodes rely on the context of having already introduced characters and relationships. The third Lion one especially loses something precious if it doesn't have the setup from numerous prior episodes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T08:16:34-07:00","id":660720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/651593-why-do-you-like-steven-universe?p=660696#post660696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Arcane is American; he can watch it legally on Cartoon Network's website. Look, it's <a href=\"http://www.cartoonnetwork.com/video/steven-universe\" target=\"_blank\">right here</a>. Oh don't do that. Most of those episodes rely on the context of having already introduced characters and relationships. The third Lion one especially loses something precious if it doesn't have the setup from numerous prior episodes.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is, Steven is an awful little shit in most of the early episodes. Which numerous prior episodes would you recommend?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T08:24:29-07:00","id":660726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/651593-why-do-you-like-steven-universe?p=660720#post660720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is, Steven is an awful little shit in most of the early episodes. Which numerous prior episodes would you recommend?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I didn't have a problem with him. What did you think was irritable about him?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013